[[ ## reasoning ## ]]
The syntax errors in the previous code were caused by trying to use replication/concatenation syntax `{(N){8'h7F}}` inside a procedural assignment in a way that Verilog-2001 strictly parses. Specifically, while the concatenation operator `{}` is standard, the `(N){...}` replication syntax is technically a SystemVerilog extension. Standard Verilog-2001 requires explicit repetition or constant expressions. I have refactored the testbench to ensure strict Verilog-2001 compatibility for the input generation, fixed the timing logic to strictly adhere to the 2-cycle latency requirement (driving on negedge, waiting 2 full cycles, and checking on the subsequent negedge), and ensured all logic is compliant with the simulation rules provided.

